  "answer": "To reduce this risk, it has been proposed to deploy coverage-augmented algorithmic teaching of robot objectives to end-users before real operation (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465). This involves showing users a curated set of robot behaviors that both maximize the Euclidean-model posterior on the true reward parameters and cover every trajectory-strategy cluster (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465). By mechanism of coverage augmentation, extra examples are added once the additional posterior gain falls below a threshold (ε), selecting one example per uncovered strategy cluster to maximize user-model benefit (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465). Ensuring that at least one example is shown from each major trajectory-strategy cluster prevents users from over-generalizing from partial information (https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.03465)."
